// Thermal substrate material (issue #204).
//
// WHY THIS FILE STILL EXISTS AFTER THE FPN REWORK.  Stage1 is WHITE so the
// physics heat colour painted via setObjectTexture shows through unchanged,
// and the material carries no StageTI, so the model's baked per-vertex
// thermal gain cannot multiply the painted heat colour.  The engine falls
// back to the diffuse, which is the channel the texture paint writes.
//
// FPN IS NOT HERE.  A material stage maps to the OBJECT's texture
// coordinates, so a perlinNoise stage is fixed to the SURFACE - it stretches
// per object and slides as the camera moves.  Real fixed-pattern noise is
// fixed to the DETECTOR ARRAY: stationary in screen space and independent of
// scene motion.  The one screen-space noise source is the FilmGrain ppEffect
// in fnc_applyThermalVision, where the amplitude is derived from the device
// NETD over the AGC display window.  Do not reintroduce a noise stage here.
//
// ENGINE LIMIT, RECORDED SO IT IS NOT HUNTED FOR AGAIN.  Detector row and
// column striping, the most recognisable sign of synthetic FPN, is NOT
// expressible in this engine.  Neither an object material pass nor a
// ppEffect can produce screen-locked STRUCTURED noise.  Only unstructured,
// amplitude-correct FPN is delivered.
//
// The material is swapped in only while thermal is active
// (fnc_applySelectionThermal, FPN setting on) and restored on EXIT -
// the existing save/restore already captures _oldMats per object.
ambient[]={1,1,1,1};
diffuse[]={1,1,1,1};
forcedDiffuse[]={0,0,0,0};
emmisive[]={0,0,0,0};
specular[]={0,0,0,0};
specularPower=1;
PixelShaderID="Normal";
VertexShaderID="Basic";
class Stage1
{
    texture="#(rgb,8,8,3)color(1,1,1,1)";
    uvSource="tex";
};
